e Ozark region of the USA.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], well-beaten\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]]\n* 1 cup chopped [[Cookbook:Nut|nuts]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to {{#invoke:temperature|f|350}}.\n# Blend all ingredients together, starting with eggs and ending with nuts.\n# Grease [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|casserole dish]], pour in casserole.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for about 35 minutes.\n# Top with [[Cookbook:Whipped Cream|whipped cream]] or ice cream.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Ozark Pudding","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 eggs, well-beaten","sourceText":"2 eggs, well-beaten","amountText":"2 eggs, well-beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 tablespoons flour","sourceText":"4 tablespoons flour","amountText":"4 tablespoons flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1½ cups brown sugar","sourceText":"1½ cups brown sugar","amountText":"1½ cups brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 teaspoons baking powder","sourceText":"3 teaspoons baking powder","amountText":"3 teaspoons baking powder","amount":null,"un